From: Marionette AirDrop driver research
Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] one bounded monitor slot then synchronous normal RX restore

0014 retained the monitor vdev and ordinary gateway RX (48/48) by restoring
the normal shared-ring layout, but monitor packet output became zero. Test
one short capture slot at a time through the existing monitor filter API,
then restore the normal layout before returning from the sysfs write.
Use the compiled monitor 1.0 setup/update path directly: the advanced-filter
CDP callback in this profile is an inline E_INVAL stub, despite being non-NULL.
Root parameter accepts 1..200 ms only, requires the default-off 0009 gate,
mission mode, an associated STA and an open driver-owned awdlmon. The vdev
operation guard and netdev reference cover the synchronous operation; no
background work/timer survives removal. Restoration is attempted on every
capture result. RAW TX and all channel policies remain unchanged.
This is a controlled timing experiment, not the completed AWDL scheduler.

